<main class="case-page"><a class="back-link" href="/work/">← ALL WORK</a><span class="eyebrow">CASE 03 / CLOUD INFRASTRUCTURE / 2026</span><h1>Three-tier AWS<br/><em>application.</em></h1><p class="case-lead">A segmented, multi-AZ application environment built with clear network and security boundaries.</p><div class="case-cover cover-sand"><div class="tier-stack"><span>PUBLIC / LOAD BALANCING</span><span>APPLICATION / COMPUTE</span><span>PRIVATE / DATA</span></div></div><div class="case-meta"><div><span>ROLE</span><b>Cloud Infrastructure</b></div><div><span>STACK</span><b>VPC · EC2 · Nginx · Tomcat · RDS MySQL</b></div><div><span>YEAR</span><b>2026</b></div></div><div class="case-content"><section><span class="eyebrow">01 / THE BRIEF</span><h2>Separate concerns.<br/><em>Limit exposure.</em></h2><p>Deploy a three-tier application across two availability zones with network segmentation and layered security groups.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">02 / THE BUILD</span><h2>Six subnets.<br/>Four security layers.</h2><p>Created public, application and data subnets across two AZs, with layered security groups, NAT gateways, Nginx, Tomcat/Spring Boot and RDS MySQL. Debugged a Tomcat 10 Jakarta migration and a ROOT webapp deployment conflict.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">03 / THE LEARNING</span><h2>Infrastructure<br/><em>is in the details.</em></h2><p>The project reinforced practical network isolation, application server troubleshooting and database access boundaries.</p><p>Keeping the database in private subnets reduces direct exposure. Separate security groups make the intended traffic path explicit: public entry, application tier and data tier. The deployment work also surfaced real application-runtime issues, including a Tomcat 10 Jakarta migration and a ROOT webapp deployment conflict.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">04 / ARCHITECTURE NOTES</span><h2>Three tiers.<br/><em>Distinct trust zones.</em></h2><p>The environment uses six subnets across two Availability Zones: public subnets for the entry layer, application subnets for compute, and private data subnets for RDS. NAT gateways support outbound access from private application resources without making the database publicly reachable.</p><p>Validation focused on the network boundaries, application-server deployment and database connectivity. This case study describes the project architecture and troubleshooting work; it does not claim a production workload or measured availability result.</p></section></div><a class="case-repo" href="https://github.com/amit-cloudops-ai/Devops-3-tire-project-001" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">VIEW SOURCE REPOSITORY ↗</a></main>
</BaseLayout>
